  "worked_solution": "The mode of a random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ is the value of $x$ at the global maxima of $f(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we can tell that $f(x)$ has a single global maximum at $x=4.$\n\nTherefore, the mode of $X$ is $4.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158570/assets/52c2514b1970553a6b4f80138e4baa6b8384d482caa447b95bd07dde5c252d11.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
